{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-bm25", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "There are four main types of coffee beans, each offering unique flavors and characteristics: Arabica, Robusta, Liberica, and Excelsa. Arabica beans are the most popular and are known for their naturally sweet taste with a light body and bright acidity, often featuring flavors like fruits, florals, nuts, and chocolate. They account for about 60% of global coffee production. Robusta beans are more bittersweet and have an earthier flavor with a heavier body, often used in espresso for their crema and richness. They are also significant in commercial production, alongside Arabica.  Liberica beans offer a unique and floral aroma with a smoky flavor, adding complexity to blends. Excelsa beans, meanwhile, are fruity and tart, contributing depth and acidity in blends. While Arabica and Robusta are the most common in supermarkets, experimenting with Liberica and Excelsa can offer new taste experiences. You can also try blends that combine these beans with Arabica to find the balance that suits your palate.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:0": 2.7182022632290455, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:1": 1.8852448548856027, "clueweb22-en0039-84-11607:2": 1.828431887112125, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:11": 1.8269682265823486, "clueweb22-en0013-60-07405:2": 1.6869212513307916, "clueweb22-en0014-27-18943:2": 1.6838995384147704, "clueweb22-en0031-65-00073:3": 1.6736248784404828, "clueweb22-en0024-35-17400:0": 1.6689840513307859, "clueweb22-en0031-65-00073:0": 1.6652935795959842, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:10": 1.6594094564875952}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I get grumpy if I don't get my coffee.", "I start my day by drinking coffee.", "I occasionally experience mild acid reflux and prefer beverages that are gentle on the stomach."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:0": 2.7182022632290455, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:1": 1.885244854885602