{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-bm25", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The finger is composed of three bones and three hinged joints, and the tendons and ligaments play crucial roles in its movement and stability. The flexor tendons in your fingers attach to muscles in your forearms and run along your finger, encased in a protective sheath made of connective tissue. The sheath has five thickened areas, known as annular pulleys (A1, A2, A3, A4, and A5), which help keep the tendon close to the bone during movement.   If your pain is tendon-related, it might be due to strain or overuse, especially if it originated from climbing, an activity involving repeated stress on this area. Climber's finger often involves issues with the tendons or pulleys.   Resting your hand and fingers, applying ice to reduce any swelling, and avoiding activities that exacerbate the pain could help. If the pain persists, consider consulting a healthcare professional for a precise diagnosis and treatment plan. They may recommend therapies or exercises that address your specific condition and help you return to climbing safely.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:1": 3.834946299928628, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:0": 3.2990242617233756, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:2": 2.6663735633489924, "clueweb22-en0034-76-16227:0": 2.3889448624128216, "clueweb22-en0012-45-12823:1": 2.3491133850952988, "clueweb22-en0030-70-18403:0": 1.9546989244587492, "clueweb22-en0005-98-01404:21": 1.8708004207166828, "clueweb22-en0012-45-12823:2": 1.7757217159812724, "clueweb22-en0013-93-15759:17": 1.6996839962544479, "clueweb22-en0016-25-19413:12": 1.6996839962544479}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors.", "Many years ago I had a bad fall while bouldering."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:1": 3.834946299928628, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:0": 3.2990242617233756, "clueweb22-en0007-15-