{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-bm25", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To effectively tape your finger for a pulley injury, use the H-taping method. This approach offers substantial support by keeping the tendons close to the bone and can help reduce strain on the injured pulley.  1. **Prepare the Tape**: Cut a piece of tape in half lengthwise from both ends, ensuring you leave a 1 cm bridge in the middle.  2. **Positioning**: Place the tape on the injured finger with the bridge located on the inside, sitting on the crease of the joint at the upper end of the injured pulley.  3. **Application**: Wrap the upper segment of the tape around the finger like a ring above the joint, and then do the same with the lower segment below the joint.  4. **Flexion Prevention**: When applying, ensure the tape restricts the finger\u2019s ability to bend at the middle joint. Flex your finger to 60\u00b0 during application to test the restriction.  5. **Re-taping**: Since tape stretches quickly, reapply it between climbing routes to maintain its effectiveness.  This method not only aids in healing by reducing movement and preventing further injury but also acts as a psychological reminder to take care while climbing.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 4.601765306769599, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:11": 4.419048204333908, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 4.399189283428764, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 4.388967759426369, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:4": 4.326565497727026, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 4.221595392453593, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 4.167531138645946, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 4.121326687779487, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:1": 4.057669775784255, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 4.0}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 4.601765306769599, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:11": 4.41904820433