{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-bm25", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "H-taping is an effective method for finger pulley injuries, offering substantial support by keeping tendons close to the bone. This technique is particularly effective in restricting finger movement and supporting injured pulleys when the fingers are flexed and under pressure. To apply H-taping, here's what you need to do:  1. Cut a length of rigid athletic tape, about 10 cm long and 1.5 cm wide. Leukoplast tape is often recommended by researchers for its effectiveness.  2. Tear the tape from each end to leave a \u00bd\u201d bridge connecting the two ends. This creates an \"H\" shape with two strips on each side.  3. With your finger straight, place the middle section (bridge) of the \"H\" along the palmar side of the joint in the middle of the finger.  4. Wrap the two ends around your finger, overlapping each side by about 50%.  The H-taping method increases crimping strength and supports the healing process by immobilizing the finger joint and reducing the range of motion, thereby preventing potential strain on the injured pulley. It's a useful method for climbers returning to the sport post-injury.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 4.619591619352431, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 4.532790151023208, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 4.31932891216835, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 4.214578418395851, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 4.007538630290796, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:11": 4.003882868329717, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 3.8214777014516645, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 3.796972930519467, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 3.6478542608515507, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 3.6345595293487563}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 4.619591619352431, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 4.532790151023208, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 4.31932891216835, "clueweb22-en0033-87-097