{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-bm25", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To prevent meetings from derailing your focus, effective preparation and scheduling are key. Start by reviewing the meeting agenda in advance, which can help you know what to expect and provide the opportunity to jot down any points you might want to address. This preparatory work ensures that you're not blindsided during the meeting and allows you to efficiently contribute to discussions, reducing potential stress or disruptions to your workflow.  If you have control over the timing of meetings, try scheduling them during periods when your focus tends to naturally wane, leaving your peak focus times open for deep, uninterrupted work. Before a meeting, you can also use a few moments to transition out of your focused work slowly, jotting down where you left off and what you'll need to pick back up, which helps maintain continuity.  Moreover, consider setting an intention for after the meeting, such as returning to a specific point in your work. This can ease the transition and help you retain your hyperfocus flow. Finally, for those post-meeting distractions, allow yourself a brief reset before diving back in, perhaps a few deep breaths or a quick physical stretch, to rejuvenate your attention.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0017-28-13846:1": 1.8770648144309958, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 1.864948744982967, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:1": 1.8411655542180263, "clueweb22-en0019-75-01093:2": 1.7913878348682344, "clueweb22-en0012-26-00836:0": 1.7337287853546717, "clueweb22-en0021-36-12826:1": 1.7105675743134703, "clueweb22-en0040-18-11535:3": 1.5895330039507396, "clueweb22-en0017-28-13846:0": 1.4456981045535295, "clueweb22-en0016-28-02016:5": 1.362658773225945, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:0": 1.2385955861677158}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0017-28-13