{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-bm25", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "When managing transitions around meetings, creating a routine can help you regain focus afterward. Here are some strategies to consider:  1. **Pre-meeting preparation:** Before a meeting, take a few minutes to jot down what you were working on. This will serve as a quick reminder when you get back to it.     2. **Mindful breaks:** Use the time before and after meetings for a short, mindful break. Stand up, stretch, or grab a drink to physically reset and mentally prepare to transition back to work mode. Since you enjoy a quiet environment, a few moments of silence could help too.  3. **Task reminders:** Set up a reminder system that cues you to the task you need to return to. This could be a visual cue on your desk or a digital reminder system.  4. **Post-meeting routine:** After the meeting, spend a few minutes reviewing your notes and plan your next steps. This helps shift your focus back without feeling lost or overwhelmed.  These practices can smooth the transition and help you quickly regain your focus with minimal disruption, especially given your ability to daydream and get lost in thought. Would you like information on any of these strategies?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0024-26-16930:4": 1.4828184220834184, "clueweb22-en0027-99-04036:9": 1.2244326432873913, "clueweb22-en0003-48-12807:1": 1.1434781988412006, "clueweb22-en0028-56-05932:1": 1.1041527510647335, "clueweb22-en0038-34-02419:14": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0028-83-13360:0": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0030-54-15087:19": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0032-22-09151:15": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0008-99-02137:5": 0.9998839674665704}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0024-26-16930:4": 1.4828184220834184, "clueweb22-en0027-99-04036:9": 1.2244326432873913, "clueweb22-en0003-48-12807:1": 1.