{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-gpt41-bm25", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The jockey refers to the small wheels in the derailleur system of your bike, known as jockey wheels. These are housed in the derailleur cage and are critical for the smooth operation of your bike's drivetrain. There are typically two jockey wheels: the guide pulley (upper wheel) and the tension pulley (lower wheel). The guide pulley helps guide the chain in the correct direction when you shift gears. It has some lateral play to accommodate slight misalignments in the chain line, ensuring smoother shifts even when the chain line isn't perfectly straight. The tension pulley is responsible for maintaining appropriate chain tension. It helps compensate for chain slack as it moves across different chainrings or cogs. By keeping the chain properly tensioned, it aids in reducing the chances of the chain slipping off, thus ensuring a more reliable ride. Adjusting or maintaining these components might help solve the chain issues you're experiencing.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 3.8956782232939835, "clueweb22-en0020-13-09241:0": 3.8241794233379034, "clueweb22-en0040-35-09091:5": 3.6046879660631843, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:2": 3.4485466845045125, "clueweb22-en0005-69-04311:0": 3.1159776437755022, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 2.9792154960689845, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:7": 2.9670415637679852, "clueweb22-en0030-00-05180:0": 2.7122909041711374, "clueweb22-en0008-19-09410:0": 2.6656120029931567, "clueweb22-en0011-34-07365:0": 2.659431737460726}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I'm a casual bike rider.", "I take my bike in the train and the bus.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 3.8956782232939835, "clueweb22-en0020-13-09241:0": 3.8241794233379034, "clueweb22-en0040-35-09091:5": 3.6046879660631843, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:2": 3.4485466845045125, "clu